  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Dean’s trailer has three tyres. At any given time two of these are used and the third is spare. The three tires have covered different distances: $25\\,000$ km, $28\\,000$ km, and $31\\,000$ km.\n\nFind the total distance that Dean’s trailer has travelled.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$42\\,000\\text{ km}$\n\nAdd the three tyre distances and divide by two, since two tyres are used at any given time.",
      "worked": "Let $d$ be the distance travelled by the trailer, in kilometres. Since two tyres are used at any given time, their combined distance is $2d$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2d &= 25\\,000+28\\,000+31\\,000\\\\2d &= 84\\,000\\\\d &= \\frac{84\\,000}{2}\\\\d &= 42\\,000\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe trailer has travelled $42\\,000\\text{ km}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
